{
  /* The Discord front's type-check program. Every compiler option below is
     `infrastructure/relay/tsconfig.json`'s byte for byte, and that file carries the argument for
     why a Worker gets a program of its own: `@cloudflare/workers-types` declares `Request`,
     `Response` and some four hundred other globals, and the app under `packages/ui/` must see the
     DOM's versions of those names and nothing else.

     A program of its own rather than a wider `include` in another Worker's, for
     `infrastructure/share-worker/tsconfig.json`'s reason: `mtg-grimoire-discord` is a deploy of
     its own, and one program spanning two Workers lets an edit to one fail the other's check.

     **Nothing of another package is in it.** The script imports no module of the relay's, and
     its tests stand D1 up over `node:sqlite` with this folder's own migration
     (`src/fake.ts`), so there is no `alias` in `wrangler.jsonc` and no dependency in
     `package.json` but the types and the runner. `src/sqlite.d.ts` declares the few names of
     `node:sqlite` the fake uses, since `types` is pinned to `@cloudflare/workers-types`.

     **`src/rpc.ts` is the one module another package reads**: the bot device's Worker
     (`infrastructure/bot-device/`) imports its types by this package's name, so the two scripts
     are checked against one interface. And `src/commands.ts` is loaded by Node as well, by
     `scripts/discord-register.ts`, so it is plain data with nothing but erasable type syntax.

     `src`'s `*.test.ts` are inside the program, as the relay's are: a test that does not
     type-check can drift from what it asserts about. `src/vite.d.ts` declares the Vite imports
     the tests read files as text by. */
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    /* No `DOM`: this is not a browser. `@cloudflare/workers-types` supplies the fetch, stream
       and URL globals workerd actually has, which are a different and smaller set. */
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "types": ["@cloudflare/workers-types"],

    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
